        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Neovim 0.12 has shipped — which was the prerequisite @justinmk mentioned before considering eager-merge of #37951.\n\nThat PR implemented exactly this (blocking `--remote` by default, `+async` opt-out) and received a positive review (\"the right shape\"), but was auto-closed by the bot after the contributor went quiet during the rebase cycle. Nothing was wrong with the approach.\n\nThe practical motivation for getting this done: `mhinz/neovim-remote` (`nvr`) has had no upstream commits since May 2022 and is effectively abandoned. Its `--remote-wait` semantics — blocking the calling process until the buffer is unloaded, needed for `$EDITOR` inside `:terminal` — is the only remaining feature native Neovim doesn't cover. Once this lands, `nvr` has no reason to exist.\n\nWould a new PR continuing from #37951's design be welcome? Happy to take it on.",
